6:{"event":"Revise","id":"F5","note":"The project's refusal doctrine, the check architecture, and where TET-28 already sits in the roadmap. README Constraints: "Refusals are format-level, never heuristic. 'You did not point at your evidence' is a decidable question. 'This looks wrong' is not, and belongs in the human-owed partition or nowhere." Two partitions, never a single document-level verdict; human-owed is "none of it is settled by a passing check, and none of it fails the run". README Direction already lists, gated on measurement: "More authoring-time refusals, where they are decidable. Requiring a workspace-rooted search behind a CLAIM THAT NAMES A SYMBOL" — i.e. the roadmap phrasing is mention-triggered — while the same section warns that "several proposed refusals have already been built, measured against a real corpus, and rejected on precision". scope.rs records exactly such a rejection for symbol-mention detection: flagging a module::symbol reference whose module never appears in the fact's captured output "would have flagged a legitimate quotation ... while missing both real overreaches"; "Naming a symbol the code you read calls is normal; concluding about what that symbol does is the failure — and those two are not distinguishable by string matching." scope.rs also states the report-vs-refusal discriminator in this project's own words: the note-outside-extent check is "human-owed, never a refusal" because "a note may legitimately name a location as context ... and only a person can tell that from an unsupported inference. Refusing would make the honest case unwritable to catch the dishonest one." Check architecture (checks.rs 1-200, report.rs 1-130): Findings holds one Vec per machine check plus human-owed lists; machine_check_failed() ORs grammar/subset/abutting/unsettled/cascade/ledger/verdict-disagreement/out-of-proof/provenance; the provenance_failed doc states the machine-partition principle — drift and an unreadable snapshot fail because "both are objective contradictions between a document and the record it claims to rest on, decidable without a human", while a MISSING snapshot is deliberately human-owed, not a failure. Snapshot-dependent findings (notes_outside_extent, mint_windows, tree_states) are "only populated when a snapshot shipped beside the memo". report.rs has a const NON_COVERAGE list printed unconditionally ("tetel does not catch: ..."), whose first entry is "dependents that never declared themselves"; exit codes 0/1/2 with 2 = no rows found, never confusable with clean.","why":"The mint folded four observations — report.rs 1-130 and checks.rs 1-200 alongside the README and scope.rs doctrine passages — and the note described only the doctrine half of its own extent. Adding what the check-architecture half actually says, verbatim where load-bearing, rather than leaving claims about it to rest on an extent the note never mentioned.","timestamp":1786131172}
88:| C12 | What the mechanism cannot catch is boundable and belongs in check's printed NON_COVERAGE list, which exists for exactly this ("a refusal that fired is easily read as coverage it never claimed"). Six entries: (a) a transplant the author never declared — no refusal can reach it; the empty section is its only trace; (b) premises the donor never wrote down — the relation selects from captured text, so a premise that lives in the donor's structure rather than its comments has nothing to select; (c) premises outside the captured extent — a donor fact that folded too narrow a look cannot yield a premise from the lines it never captured; (d) shallow selection — the tool verifies that selected bytes are the donor's, never that they are all the load-bearing ones; selecting one convenient clause and stopping is invisible to any format-level check: "what counts as a premise is design judgment" is a boundary the ticket itself draws and this design records as the ticket's stipulation, and deciding a selection is too small is a truth-check, the insincere-examination ceiling this project registered as permanently out of reach; (e) whether the discharge claim actually addresses its premise, and whether the cited target really is the mechanism's destination — both content; the claim is graded by a grounding pass as written, and the linkage is graded by nobody; (f) a donor comment that is itself wrong — verbatim quotation establishes provenance, never truth. None of these is reachable by a format-level refusal, so printing them is the honest disposition, not a fallback. | OWED |
90:| C14 | The implementation surface is small and every piece extends a mechanism already in the tree: one serde-defaulted per-entry output-length field on ExtentEntry (the same compatibility precedent that added kind and pattern, with the same absent-means-ineligible reading); one new record kind with its counter and id prefix; one transplants.jsonl appended by one CLI/MCP-shared dispatch, shipped by adding one line to snapshot.rs's deliberately-enumerated SNAPSHOT_FILES (whose targets.jsonl entry already documents why a record log must ship: without it the refusal "would hold only inside the workspace that authored the memo"); one rendered section beside render_targets; one completeness refusal in the render --out path; one check re-verifying from files the snapshot already carries (transplant machine findings beside uncensused_targets, unverifiable rows human-owed without a snapshot); and the new NON_COVERAGE lines. Nothing parses any programming language, nothing is re-run at check time, and no aggregate, score, or document-level verdict is introduced anywhere. | OWED |
104:| F7 | The assembly-and-verification surfaces TET-29 extends, first-hand. compose.rs: render appends render_targets between the prose and the evidence ledger; the section renders "None declared..." once any claim exists ("the hole is the finding" — "an absent section would make the same omission invisible, which is the failure mode, not the fix"); withdrawn targets are dropped, live ones render as a two-column table \|`symbol`\|F#\|; only labels are rendered, never absolute keys ("a committed document should not carry /Users/<someone>/..."), and captured output is deliberately NOT rendered into the document ("unbounded ... it is in the snapshot for anyone who needs it, and a document that inlined it would bury the prose"). checks.rs: Findings has uncensused_targets as a MACHINE failure ("re-verified against the shipped snapshot ... what this catches is the document that never passed through that verb: hand-authored, edited after rendering, or carrying a target row its own snapshot does not have. Both directions are checked"), and unverifiable_targets as human-owed when no snapshot shipped; machine_check_failed() ORs grammar/subset/abutting/unsettled/cascade/ledger/verdict-disagreement/out-of-proof/uncensused-targets/provenance; out_of_proof (every record grades a wording the claim no longer carries) is a machine failure whose remedy is reproving. report.rs: exit codes 0/1/2; NON_COVERAGE is a const list printed item by item ("tetel does not catch: ..."), and TET-28 added five census entries to it with a comment explaining why ("a refusal that fired is easily read as coverage it never claimed"); first entry is "dependents that never declared themselves". | /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/compose.rs lines 1-130; /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/checks.rs lines 120-215; /Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/report.rs lines 13-40 | C9, C11, C12, C13, C14 |
