3:{"event":"Create","id":"F3","note":"What survives from an observation into a fact and its snapshot. pending.rs: PendingEntry carries kind (ObservationKind: Path | GrepMatch | NoMatch | Proc), key, label, output, world_root, world_state, captured_at. facts.rs mint(): the fold copies ONLY key, label, world_root, world_state into ExtentEntry — the kind is dropped, and a grep's pattern exists nowhere except inside the display label text ("no-match: <pattern> in <root>", "<file> (grep: <pattern>)"). Two schema-evolution precedents matter for extending this: (a) world_root is #[serde(default)] for entries minted before it existed, and an empty root is deliberately read as "comparable with nothing" — "check treats it that way rather than guessing"; (b) facts.jsonl ships in the snapshot with full extent entries (mint_windows reads the snapshot's facts.jsonl, and its doc says the Create timestamp "ships in facts.jsonl, and the snapshot copies refusals.log beside it"). Also: there is deliberately no flag on fact's surface that lets a caller supply extent or captured output — "that absence is the guarantee that a fact was actually backed by a look/run". Extent, output and pin are set once at mint and no revision event can carry them.","extent":[{"key":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/pending.rs","label":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/pending.rs","world_root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","world_state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"},{"key":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/facts.rs","label":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel/src/facts.rs","world_root":"/Volumes/SSD/Documents/lonic/tetel","world_state":"git:7c8965b105b644cbdac2f4f631373fd31ab2e7f8805fa51cb26d60e9746c7db2"}],"output":"//! The pending observation buffer: what `tetel look`/`tetel run` fill,
//! and what `tetel fact` mints from. Persisted as a single JSON file per
